  "question": {
    "text": "If the roots of the equation $b x^2+c x+a=0$ be imaginary, then for all real values of $x$, the expression $3 b^2 x^2+6 b c x+2 c^2$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "MYC6r",
      "text": "\ngreater than $4 a b$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HyTrW",
      "text": "\nless than $4 a b$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "OgG8C",
      "text": "\ngreater than $-4 a b$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "DScHm",
      "text": "\nless than - 4ab",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\nb x^2+c x+a=0\n$$\nRoots are imaginary $\\Rightarrow c^2-4 a b < 0 \\Rightarrow c^2 < 4 a b \\Rightarrow-c^2>-4 a b$ $3 b^2 x^2+6 b c x+2 c^2$\nsince $3 b^2>0$\nGiven expression has minimum value\nMinimum value $=\\frac{4\\left(3 b^2\\right)\\left(2 c^2\\right)-36 b^2 c^2}{4\\left(3 b^2\\right)}=-\\frac{12 b^2 c^2}{12 b^2}=-c^2>-4 a b$.",
    "image": null
  },
